#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:1
msgid ""
"PLUMED Masterclass 22.13: SASA module and the application of PLUMED for "
"implicit solvent simulations"
msgstr ""
"PLUMED Masterclass 22.13：SASA Module と Implicit Solvent シミュレーションへの PLUMED "
"の適用"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:3
msgid "Origin"
msgstr "作成について"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:5
msgid "This masterclass was authored by Andrea Arsiccio on September 12, 2022"
msgstr "この Masterclass は、2022年9月12日に Andrea Arsiccio によって作成された。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:7
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:9
msgid ""
"This Masterclass is an introduction to the use of the SASA module of Plumed "
"for the execution of implicit solvent simulations."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass では、Plumed の SASA Module を使う Implicit Solvent シミュレーションを紹介します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:11
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:13
msgid "The objectives of this Masterclass are:"
msgstr "この Masterclass の到達目標は次のとおりである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:14
msgid "Learn how the SASA module of PLUMED works"
msgstr "PLUMED の SASA Module の仕組みを学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:15
msgid ""
"Learn how to run an implicit solvent simulation of a protein using PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED でタンパク質の Implicit Solvent シミュレーションを実行する方法を学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid ""
"Learn how to introduce the effect of temperature, pressure and osmolytes on "
"protein stability in implicit solvent simulations"
msgstr "Implicit Solvent シミュレーションにおけるタンパク質の安定性に、温度・圧力・Osmolyte の影響を導入する方法を学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:17
msgid ""
"Understand the advantages and limitations of implicit solvent simulations "
"using PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED による Implicit Solvent シミュレーションの利点と限界を理解する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:19
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "前提条件"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:21
msgid ""
"We assume that the person that will follow this tutorial is familiar with "
"the Linux terminal, AMBER and basic functionality of PLUMED. Knowledge of "
"the metadynamics enhanced sampling technique is recommended. Familiarity "
"with gnuplot and xmgrace (or python with matplotlib) is recommended."
msgstr ""
"Linux Terminal、AMBER、PLUMED の基本機能に慣れていることを前提とします。Enhanced Sampling 法である "
"Metadynamics の知識と、gnuplot、xmgrace（または Python と matplotlib）の使用経験を推奨します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:25
msgid "Setting up PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED のセットアップ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:27
msgid ""
"We will use AMBER and PLUMED to perform the calculations. Conda packages "
"with the software required for this class have been prepared and you can "
"install them following the instructions in [this "
"link](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-2022). Make sure to install the "
"conda package for AMBER."
msgstr ""
"計算には AMBER と PLUMED を使います。必要なソフトウェアの conda Package "
"が用意されており、[こちら](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-2022) "
"の手順でインストールできます。AMBER の conda Package も忘れずにインストールしてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:31
msgid ""
"If you are compiling PLUMED on your own, you will need to install the SASA "
"module manually by adding '--enable-modules=sasa' to your './configure' "
"command when building PLUMED."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED を自分でコンパイルする場合は、ビルド時の './configure' コマンドに '--enable-modules=sasa' "
"を追加し、SASA Module を手動で有効にする必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:33
msgid ""
"The data needed to run the exercises of this Masterclass can be found on "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/masterclass-22-13). You can "
"clone this repository locally on your machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"演習に必要なデータは [GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/masterclass-22-13) "
"にあります。次のコマンドでリポジトリを自分のマシンに Clone できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:40
msgid ""
"You will also need a python script for the calculation of free energies of "
"transfer, available on [GitHub] (https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/DeltaG-"
"calculation)."
msgstr ""
"移行自由エネルギーの計算用 Python スクリプトも必要です。[GitHub] (https://github.com/andrea-"
"arsiccio/DeltaG-calculation) で入手できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:42
msgid "Summary of theory"
msgstr "理論のまとめ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:44
msgid ""
"The SASA module contains methods for the calculation of the solvent "
"accessible surface area (SASA) of proteins. It can be used to include the "
"SASA as a collective variable in metadynamics simulations, and for implicit "
"solvent simulations."
msgstr ""
"SASA Module には、タンパク質の Solvent Accessible Surface Area (SASA) "
"を計算する方法が含まれます。Metadynamics で SASA を Collective Variable として使う場合や、Implicit "
"Solvent シミュレーションに利用できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:47
msgid "There are two SASA functions that could be used:"
msgstr "使用できる SASA 関数は2つあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:49
msgid ""
"SASA_HASEL: computates the SASA using the algorithm described "
"[here](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0898552988900152)"
msgstr ""
"SASA_HASEL：[こちら](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0898552988900152)"
" のアルゴリズムで SASA を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:51
msgid ""
"SASA_LCPO: computes the SASA using the algorithm described "
"[here](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/%28SICI%291096-987X%2819990130%2920%3A2%3C217%3A%3AAID-"
"JCC4%3E3.0.CO%3B2-A)"
msgstr ""
"SASA_LCPO：[こちら](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/%28SICI%291096-987X%2819990130%2920%3A2%3C217%3A%3AAID-"
"JCC4%3E3.0.CO%3B2-A) のアルゴリズムで SASA を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:53
msgid ""
"The algorithm by Hasel et al. is about 2 to 3 times faster than the LCPO "
"(linear combination of pairwise overlaps) algorithm, but slightly less "
"accurate. Both algorithms have the advantage that apply simple analytical "
"functions for the computation of the SASA, and because of this it is easy to"
" compute their derivative, which is a necessary step to apply a bias based "
"on the SASA to a molecular dynamics simulation."
msgstr ""
"Hasel らのアルゴリズムは LCPO (Linear Combination of Pairwise Overlaps) "
"より約2〜3倍高速ですが、精度は少し低くなります。どちらも簡単な解析関数で SASA を計算するため、微分を容易に計算できます。これは、SASA "
"に基づく Bias を Molecular Dynamics に適用するために必要です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:55
msgid ""
"The atoms for which the SASA is desired should be indicated with the keyword"
" ATOMS, and a pdb file of the protein must be provided in input with the "
"MOLINFO keyword. Two types of calculations are possible:"
msgstr ""
"SASA を求める原子を Keyword ATOMS で指定し、タンパク質の pdb ファイルを MOLINFO "
"で入力します。計算には2つの種類があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:57
msgid ""
"TOTAL: the total SASA is computed, which is the desired type of calculation "
"if one wants to use the SASA as a CV in metadynamics simulations."
msgstr "TOTAL：全 SASA を計算します。Metadynamics で SASA を CV として使う場合に選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:59
msgid ""
"TRANSFER: in this case the free energy of transfer for the protein is "
"computed according to the transfer model (TRANSFER). This keyword can be "
"used, for instance, to compute:"
msgstr ""
"TRANSFER：Transfer Model (TRANSFER) に従ってタンパク質の移行自由エネルギーを計算します。例えば次の計算に使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:61
msgid ""
"The transfer of a protein to different temperatures as in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694)"
msgstr ""
"[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694) "
"のような、異なる温度へのタンパク質の移行。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:62
msgid ""
"The transfer of a protein to different pressures as in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c04398)"
msgstr ""
"[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c04398) "
"のような、異なる圧力へのタンパク質の移行。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:63
msgid ""
"The transfer of a protein to different osmolyte solutions as in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.2c00889)"
msgstr ""
"[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.2c00889) のような、異なる "
"Osmolyte 溶液へのタンパク質の移行。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:65
msgid ""
"Using the protein SASA as a CV in metadynamics simulations, or monitoring "
"the SASA on the fly during the simulation or while postprocessing a "
"trajectory, is straightforward. The user, after having enabled the SASA "
"module, can use the SASA functions mentioned above similarly to any other CV"
" in PLUMED."
msgstr ""
"タンパク質の SASA を Metadynamics の CV に使うことや、シミュレーション中または Trajectory の後処理で SASA "
"を監視することは簡単です。SASA Module を有効にすれば、上記の SASA 関数を PLUMED のほかの CV と同様に使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:67
msgid ""
"For instance, the following input tells plumed to print the total SASA for "
"atoms 10 to 20 in a protein chain:"
msgstr "例えば次の入力は、タンパク質鎖の原子10〜20の全 SASA を出力するよう plumed に指示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:74
msgid ""
"This tutorial will focus on the use of the SASA module for running implicit "
"solvent simulations with PLUMED. In implicit solvent simulations, the "
"solvent is not any more described at atomistic/coarse-grained level, but is "
"instead treated as a continuum and described as a mean field. The advantages"
" are that the absence of the solvent degrees of freedom alleviates the "
"computational cost, and the absence of viscous friction accelerates the "
"exploration of the protein conformational space. However, the solvent "
"effects are described less accurately. The degree of accuracy can be "
"improved by using the concept of free energy of transfer, which is at the "
"basis of the SASA module."
msgstr ""
"この Tutorial では、SASA Module を使って PLUMED で Implicit Solvent "
"シミュレーションを実行します。Implicit Solvent では、溶媒を原子・Coarse-grained レベルで記述せず、連続体として Mean"
" Field で記述します。溶媒の自由度がないため計算コストが低く、粘性摩擦もないためタンパク質の Conformational Space "
"の探索が速くなる利点があります。一方、溶媒効果の記述精度は低下します。SASA Module "
"の基礎となる移行自由エネルギーの概念を使うと、精度を改善できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:78
msgid ""
"The common implementation of implicit solvent simulations relies on the "
"computation of the free energy of a protein as the sum of three "
"contributions:"
msgstr "一般的な Implicit Solvent シミュレーションの実装では、タンパク質の自由エネルギーを3つの寄与の和として計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:84
msgid ""
"where $E^{vac}$ is the molecule's energy in vacuum, which is the sum of "
"internal contributions (bond and angle stretching, dihedral angles "
"interactions) and van der Waals energy terms. $G^{np}$ is the non-polar "
"solvation contribution, i.e., the free energy of solvation for a molecule "
"from which all charges have been removed. $G^{el}$ is the electrostatic "
"part, calculated as the free energy for turning on the partial charges in "
"solution. This approach has been developed to describe (implicitly) the "
"solvation of a protein in pure water, at ambient temperature (298 K) and "
"pressure (1 atm)."
msgstr ""
"$E^{vac}$ は真空中の分子のエネルギーで、内部寄与（結合・角度の伸縮、Dihedral Angle の相互作用）と van der Waals "
"エネルギー項の和です。$G^{np}$ は Non-polar Solvation の寄与、すなわちすべての電荷を除いた分子の Solvation "
"自由エネルギーです。$G^{el}$ は静電的な部分で、溶液中で Partial Charge "
"を有効にする自由エネルギーとして計算します。この方法は、常温 (298 K)・常圧 (1 atm) の純水中でのタンパク質の Solvation "
"を暗黙的に記述するために開発されました。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:86
msgid ""
"The idea behind the SASA module is the addition of a free energy of transfer"
" term $G^{tr}(T,P,c)$:"
msgstr "SASA Module の考え方は、移行自由エネルギー項 $G^{tr}(T,P,c)$ を追加することです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:92
msgid ""
"that describes the transfer of the protein to any given temperature $T$, "
"pressure $P$ and concentration $c$ of an osmolyte."
msgstr "これは、任意の温度 $T$、圧力 $P$、Osmolyte 濃度 $c$ へのタンパク質の移行を記述します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:94
msgid "The free energy of transfer term has the following functional form:"
msgstr "移行自由エネルギー項は、次の関数形を持ちます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:100
msgid ""
"where $n$ is the number of residues in the protein and the global transfer "
"free energy is obtained by summing the contributions ($g^{tr}$) given by the"
" amino acid side chains (subscript sc) and by the peptide backbone "
"(subscript bb)."
msgstr ""
"$n$ はタンパク質の残基数です。アミノ酸側鎖（添字 sc）と Peptide Backbone（添字 bb）の寄与 ($g^{tr}$) "
"を足し合わせて全体の移行自由エネルギーを求めます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:102
msgid ""
"Each contribution is weighed by the fractional solvent accessible surface "
"area $SASA_{j}$ of residue $j$,"
msgstr "各寄与は、残基 $j$ の Solvent Accessible Surface Area の比 $SASA_{j}$ で重み付けします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:108
msgid ""
"where $SASA_{j, Gly-X-Gly}$ is the solvent accessibility of amino acid X in "
"the tripeptide Gly-X-Gly, and X is the amino acid residue type $j$."
msgstr ""
"$SASA_{j, Gly-X-Gly}$ は Tripeptide Gly-X-Gly 内のアミノ酸 X の Solvent "
"Accessibility で、X は残基 $j$ のアミノ酸種です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:110
msgid ""
"The amino acid side chains and peptide backbone contributions to the "
"transfer free energy are computed according to the mathematical derivation "
"described in the papers above."
msgstr "アミノ酸側鎖と Peptide Backbone の移行自由エネルギーへの寄与は、上記の論文の数学的導出に従って計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:112
msgid ""
"Briefly, the tranfer free energy contributions describing the effect of "
"temperatures have been derived by downloading a large set of Protein Data "
"Bank (pdb) files resolved by nuclear magnetic resonance at different "
"temperatures, and by computing the probability of different side "
"chains/backbone groups to be surface exposed at different temperatures. The "
"relation between energy and probability has then been exploited to compute "
"the free energy of transfer contributions as a function of temperature."
msgstr ""
"簡単にいうと、温度効果を表す移行自由エネルギーの寄与は、異なる温度の Nuclear Magnetic Resonance で決定された多数の "
"Protein Data Bank (pdb) ファイルを取得し、側鎖・Backbone "
"基が各温度で表面に露出する確率を計算して導出しました。エネルギーと確率の関係から、移行自由エネルギーの寄与を温度の関数として求めています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:115
msgid ""
"The transfer free energy terms describing the effect of pressure have been "
"obtained by computing three different contributions for each side "
"chain/backbone group: 1) the elimination of a consistent fraction of the "
"void volumes that are present within the native state upon unfolding, 2) the"
" volume reduction of bound water molecules due to the increased SASA of a "
"protein upon unfolding, and 3) the stabilizing excluded volume effect of a "
"denser solvent."
msgstr ""
"圧力効果を表す移行自由エネルギー項は、各側鎖・Backbone 基について3つの寄与を計算して求めました。1）Unfolding に伴う Native "
"State 内の空隙体積の一定割合の消失、2）Unfolding による SASA 増加に伴う結合水分子の体積減少、3）密度の高い溶媒による安定化の "
"Excluded Volume 効果です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:117
msgid ""
"Finally, the transfer free energy contributions as function of osmolyte "
"type/concentrations have been obtained from experimental works, where "
"solubility measurements of protein amino acids/peptide backbone models have "
"been conducted in different osmolyte solutions and exploited to extract the "
"difference in chemical potential between water and the osmolyte solution "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"最後に、Osmolyte の種類・濃度に対する移行自由エネルギーの寄与は、実験研究から得ています。異なる Osmolyte "
"溶液中でタンパク質のアミノ酸・Peptide Backbone モデルの溶解度を測定し、水と Osmolyte 溶液の化学ポテンシャル差を抽出します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:119
msgid ""
"The interested user is invited to read the original works on this topic, "
"which are included in the graph illustrating this tutorial, for a better "
"understanding of the theory behind the free energy of transfer "
"contributions."
msgstr "移行自由エネルギーの寄与の理論をよりよく理解するため、この Tutorial の Graph にある原著論文を読んでください。"

