msgstr ""
"TRANSFER を使う場合、側鎖と Backbone 原子の移行自由エネルギー ($g^{tr}$) の値を含むファイルを DELTAGFILE "
"で指定します。形式は次のとおりです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:150
msgid ""
"where the second column is the free energy of transfer for each "
"sidechain/backbone, in kJ/mol."
msgstr "第2列は、各側鎖・Backbone の移行自由エネルギーで、単位は kJ/mol です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:152
msgid ""
"A Python script for the computation of free energy of transfer values to "
"describe the effect of osmolyte concentration, temperature and pressure "
"(using ideas from the papers that are cited above) is freely available on "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/DeltaG-calculation). The script "
"automatically outputs a DeltaG.dat file compatible with the SASA module. "
"Please have a look at the README file of this script to better understand "
"its usage."
msgstr ""
"Osmolyte 濃度・温度・圧力の影響を記述する移行自由エネルギーの計算用 Python スクリプトが "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/DeltaG-calculation) "
"で無料公開されています。上記論文の考え方を使い、SASA Module に対応する DeltaG.dat を自動出力します。使い方はスクリプトの "
"README を確認してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:154
msgid ""
"For instance, the following input tells plumed to compute the transfer free "
"energy for the protein chain containing atoms 10 to 20. Such transfer free "
"energy is then used as a bias in the simulation (e.g., implicit solvent "
"simulations). The free energy of transfer values are read from a file called"
" DeltaG.dat:"
msgstr ""
"例えば次の入力は、原子10〜20を含むタンパク質鎖の移行自由エネルギーを plumed で計算します。これをシミュレーション（Implicit "
"Solvent など）の Bias として使います。移行自由エネルギーの値は DeltaG.dat から読み込みます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:164
msgid ""
"If the DELTAGFILE is not provided, the SASA module computes the free energy "
"of transfer values as if they had to take into account the effect of "
"temperature according to approaches 2 or 3 (they differ in the mathematical "
"model employed to extract free energies of transfer) in the paper about "
"using SASA with temperature. Please read and cite this paper if using the "
"transfer model for computing the effect of temperature in implicit solvent "
"simulations. For this purpose, the keyword APPROACH should be added, and set"
" to either 2 or 3, as exemplified in the following input:"
msgstr ""
"DELTAGFILE を指定しない場合、SASA Module は温度に SASA を使う論文の Approach "
"2または3に従って、温度効果を考慮する移行自由エネルギーを計算します。両者は移行自由エネルギーを抽出する数学モデルが異なります。Implicit "
"Solvent の温度効果に Transfer Model を使う場合は、この論文を読んで引用してください。次の例のように APPROACH "
"を追加し、2または3を設定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:174
msgid "The system: Refolding of a model peptide"
msgstr "対象系：モデル Peptide の Refolding"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:176
msgid ""
"For this tutorial we will work on a model peptide called $(AAQAA)\\_3$. "
"$(AAQAA)\\_3$ is a short peptide with known $\\alpha$-helix structure. We "
"will simulate this peptide starting from an unfolded conformation, and we "
"will see in which conditions (of temperature, pressure, and solution "
"composition) it folds back to a $\\alpha$-helix, and which conditions "
"promote instead an unfolded conformation."
msgstr ""
"この Tutorial では $(AAQAA)\\_3$ というモデル Peptide を使います。$(AAQAA)\\_3$ は、既知の "
"$\\alpha$-helix 構造を持つ短い Peptide です。Unfolded Conformation から開始し、どの温度・圧力・溶液組成で"
" $\\alpha$-helix に戻り、どの条件で Unfolded Conformation が促進されるかを調べます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:179
msgid ""
"[Starting (unfolded) conformation of the model peptide used for the "
"simulations](figs/masterclass-22-13-aaqaa_min.png)"
msgstr ""
"[シミュレーションに使うモデル Peptide の初期 Unfolded "
"Conformation](figs/masterclass-22-13-aaqaa_min.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:181
msgid ""
"We will perform the simulations in implicit solvent, using the AMBER ff03 "
"force field."
msgstr "AMBER ff03 Force Field を使い、Implicit Solvent で実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:183
msgid "For this tutorial, the following conditions will be explored:"
msgstr "この Tutorial では次の条件を調べます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:185
msgid "298 K, 1 bar, 0 M"
msgstr "298 K, 1 bar, 0 M"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:186
msgid ""
"228 K (approach 2 in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694)), 1 bar, 0 M"
msgstr ""
"228 K（[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694) の "
"Approach 2）, 1 bar, 0 M"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:187
msgid ""
"348 K (approach 2 in [this "
"paper](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694)), 1 bar, 0 M"
msgstr ""
"348 K（[この論文](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/acs.jpcb.1c01694) の "
"Approach 2）, 1 bar, 0 M"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:188
msgid "298 K, 1 bar, 10 M urea"
msgstr "298 K, 1 bar, 10 M urea"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:189
msgid "298 K, 3 kbar, 0 M"
msgstr "298 K, 3 kbar, 0 M"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:191
msgid "Each simulation will be performed for 5 ns."
msgstr "各シミュレーションは5 ns 実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:193
msgid ""
"Exercise 1: Simulation 1 at 298 K, 1 bar and 0 M osmolyte concentration"
msgstr "演習1：298 K、1 bar、Osmolyte 濃度0 M のシミュレーション1"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:195
msgid ""
"For the exercises, we will need PLUMED and AMBER. For this purpose, you "
"should first proceed to their installation using the provided conda "
"packages:"
msgstr "演習には PLUMED と AMBER が必要です。まず付属の conda Package でインストールしてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:216
msgid ""
"Then, you should download the folder with the input files for the exercises "
"using the following command:"
msgstr "次のコマンドで演習用入力ファイルのフォルダをダウンロードします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:222
msgid ""
"In order to perform exercise 1, cd to the folder SASA_module/01_298K. There "
"you will find a number of files:"
msgstr "演習1では SASA_module/01_298K に cd してください。次のファイルがあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:224
msgid ""
"-aaqaa.prmtop: a topology file of the protein, described according to the "
"AMBER ff03 force field."
msgstr "-aaqaa.prmtop：AMBER ff03 Force Field で記述したタンパク質の Topology。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:226
msgid ""
"-AAQAA_298.in: an input file for running the simulation through AMBER. I "
"will go more in detail over this file in the following."
msgstr "-AAQAA_298.in：AMBER でシミュレーションを実行する入力ファイル。後で詳しく説明します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:228
msgid ""
"-aaqaa_min.ncrst/aaqaa_min.pdb: configuration files for the (unfolded) "
"protein, which we will use as starting point for our simulations."
msgstr ""
"-aaqaa_min.ncrst/aaqaa_min.pdb：シミュレーションの初期状態に使う Unfolded タンパク質の "
"Configuration ファイル。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:230
msgid ""
"-histograms.py/picture_rg_alpha.gnu/script_rg_alpha.bash: files that we will"
" use for the analyses and postprocessing of our trajectories."
msgstr ""
"-histograms.py/picture_rg_alpha.gnu/script_rg_alpha.bash：Trajectory "
"の解析・後処理に使うファイル。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:232
msgid ""
"-plumed.dat: PLUMED input file. I will go more in detail over this in the "
"following."
msgstr "-plumed.dat：PLUMED 入力ファイル。後で詳しく説明します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:234
msgid ""
"The AAQAA_298.in file is an input AMBER file for carrying out our implicit "
"solvent simulation, and it has the following aspect:"
msgstr "AAQAA_298.in は、Implicit Solvent シミュレーション用の AMBER 入力で、次の内容です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:248
msgid "where the different commands have the following meaning:"
msgstr "各コマンドの意味は次のとおりです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:250
msgid ""
"imin = 0: we are running an MD simulation without performing energy "
"minimization"
msgstr "imin = 0：Energy Minimization を行わず MD を実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:251
msgid ""
"igb = 5: we are using the model described "
"[here](https://doi.org/10.1002/prot.20033) for computing the electrostatic "
"interactions $G^{el}$"
msgstr ""
"igb = 5：[こちら](https://doi.org/10.1002/prot.20033) のモデルで静電相互作用 $G^{el}$ "
"を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:252
msgid "gbsa = 1: the $G^{np}$ term is also computed"
msgstr "gbsa = 1：$G^{np}$ 項も計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:253
msgid "extdiel = 78.4: the dielectric constant of the solvent"
msgstr "extdiel = 78.4：溶媒の誘電率。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:254
msgid "ntpr = 1000: we print energy info every 1000 steps"
msgstr "ntpr = 1000：1000 Step ごとにエネルギー情報を出力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:255
msgid "ntwx = 1000: we print coordinates every 1000 steps"
msgstr "ntwx = 1000：1000 Step ごとに座標を出力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:256
msgid "ntwr = 1000: we print the restart file every 1000 steps"
msgstr "ntwr = 1000：1000 Step ごとに再開用ファイルを出力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:257
msgid "ntt = 3: we apply Langevin dynamics"
msgstr "ntt = 3：Langevin Dynamics を適用します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:258
msgid "gamma_ln = 1.0: we set the collision frequency for Langevin dynamics"
msgstr "gamma_ln = 1.0：Langevin Dynamics の Collision Frequency を設定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:259
msgid ""
"ig = -1: seed for pseudo-random number generator. -1 means that the random "
"seed will be based on the current date and time"
msgstr "ig = -1：疑似乱数生成の Seed。-1の場合、現在の日付・時刻に基づく Random Seed を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:260
msgid ""
"nscm = 500: translational/rotational COM motions will be removed every 500 "
"steps"
msgstr "nscm = 500：500 Step ごとに COM の並進・回転運動を除去します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:261
msgid "tempi = 298.0: initial temperature"
msgstr "tempi = 298.0：初期温度。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:262
msgid "temp0 = 298.0: reference temperature at which the system is to be kept"
msgstr "temp0 = 298.0：系を維持する基準温度。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:263
msgid "nstlim = 2500000: we will run the system for 2500000 steps"
msgstr "nstlim = 2500000：2500000 Step 実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:264
msgid "dt = 0.002: we will apply a 2 fs time step"
msgstr "dt = 0.002：Time Step を2 fs とします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:265
msgid "ntc = 2: we will constrain bonds linking to a hydrogen"
msgstr "ntc = 2：水素につながる結合を拘束します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:266
msgid ""
"ntf = 2: bond interactions involving H-atoms will be omitted in force "
"evaluations"
msgstr "ntf = 2：力の評価で H 原子を含む結合相互作用を省略します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:267
msgid "cut = 9999.0: no cut off will be applied for nonbonded interactions"
msgstr "cut = 9999.0：Nonbonded 相互作用に Cutoff を適用しません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:268
msgid "plumed = 1: we will run PLUMED together with AMBER"
msgstr "plumed = 1：AMBER とともに PLUMED を実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:269
msgid ""
"plumedfile = 'plumed.dat': the PLUMED file to read is called plumed.dat"
msgstr "plumedfile = 'plumed.dat'：読み込む PLUMED ファイルは plumed.dat です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:271
msgid "The PLUMED input file plumed.dat has, instead, the following aspect:"
msgstr "一方、PLUMED 入力 plumed.dat は次の内容です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:296
msgid ""
"We are providing PLUMED with a protein structure (aaqaa_min.pdb) in input "
"using the MOLINFO keyword. We are then computing the radius of gyration, "
"parallel/antiparallel beta-sheet content and alpha-helix content of the "
"protein, and we are printing this info to a file called COLVAR every 1000 "
"integration steps. $(AAQAA)\\_3$ should fold as a alpha-helix, but we are "
"monitoring also the parallel/antiparallel beta-sheet content in order to "
"identify potential cases of misfolding."
msgstr ""
"MOLINFO でタンパク質構造 (aaqaa_min.pdb) を入力します。Radius of "
"Gyration、Parallel/Antiparallel Beta-sheet の含有量、Alpha-helix の含有量を計算し、1000 "
"Integration Step ごとに COLVAR に出力します。$(AAQAA)\\_3$ は Alpha-helix に Fold "
"するはずですが、Misfolding の可能性を見つけるため、Parallel/Antiparallel Beta-sheet の含有量も監視します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:300
msgid ""
"In this first example, we are simulating $(AAQAA)\\_3$ in pure water at 298 "
"K and ambient pressure, so we do not need to add the free energy of transfer"
" term $G^{tr}(T,P,c)$, and the SASA module is not even called in the PLUMED "
"file. However, for exercises 2-5, you will need to use the SASA module to "
"include the effect of temperature/pressure/urea concentration on protein "
"stability."
msgstr ""
"最初の例では、298 K・常圧の純水中で $(AAQAA)\\_3$ をシミュレーションするため、移行自由エネルギー項 $G^{tr}(T,P,c)$ "
"は不要で、PLUMED 入力は SASA Module を呼び出しません。ただし演習2〜5では、温度・圧力・urea "
"濃度がタンパク質の安定性に与える影響を導入するため SASA Module を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:303
msgid "To run the simulation, just type the command:"
msgstr "次のコマンドでシミュレーションを実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:309
msgid ""
"The simulation should take 1-2 hours on a common laptop, so you should not "
"need a cluster for this masterclass."
msgstr "一般的な Laptop で1〜2時間程度なので、この Masterclass に Cluster は不要でしょう。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:311
msgid ""
"At the end of the simulation, you will have a COLVAR file that lists the "
"evolution of radius of gyration and secondary structure content of the "
"protein as function of time. Try to plot the columns of the COLVAR file "
"versus time."
msgstr ""
"終了時の COLVAR には、タンパク質の Radius of Gyration と Secondary Structure "
"含有量の時間変化が記録されます。各列を時間に対して描画してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:313
msgid ""
"Does the protein fold? If yes, how fast is the process? Do you think the "
"process would be equally fast in explicit solvent?"
msgstr "タンパク質は Fold しますか？するとしたら、どれほど速いですか？Explicit Solvent でも同じ速さになるでしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:315
msgid ""
"Here is the evolution of the helical content of $(AAQAA)\\_3$ over time "
"during the simulation:"
msgstr "シミュレーション中の $(AAQAA)\\_3$ の Helix 含有量の時間変化を示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:317
msgid ""
"[Evolution of helical content over time during the simulation of exercise "
"1](figs/masterclass-22-13-tvsalpha.png)"
msgstr "[演習1のシミュレーション中の Helix 含有量の時間変化](figs/masterclass-22-13-tvsalpha.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:319
msgid ""
"You can also use the script_rg_alpha.bash file provided to have a 2D "
"representation of the conformational space explored by the protein during "
"the simulation. Just type:"
msgstr ""
"付属の script_rg_alpha.bash で、シミュレーション中にタンパク質が探索した Conformational Space "
"を2次元で表せます。次のように入力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:326
msgid ""
"The script generates a file called normFEL.dat that can be visualized in "
"gnuplot using the picture_rg_alpha.gnu script provided. You should obtain "
"something similar to:"
msgstr ""
"生成される normFEL.dat は、付属の picture_rg_alpha.gnu で gnuplot "
"に表示できます。次のような結果になるはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:328
msgid ""
"[Free energy surface showing radius of gyration and helical content of the "
"protein during the simulation of exercise "
"1](figs/masterclass-22-13-FES_rg_alpha.png)"
msgstr ""
"[演習1でのタンパク質の Radius of Gyration と Helix "
"含有量を表す自由エネルギー表面](figs/masterclass-22-13-FES_rg_alpha.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:330
msgid ""
"Exercises 2-5: Introducing the free energy of transfer contribution to "
"implicit solvent simulations"
msgstr "演習2〜5：Implicit Solvent シミュレーションへの移行自由エネルギーの導入"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:332
msgid ""
"Using the learnings from the theoretical part of this masterclass and "
"exercise 1, you should now be able to autonomously run exercises 2-5. The "
"difference now is that you need to employ free energy of transfer "
"contributions to simulate the solution conditions of exercises 2-5. "
"Exercises 2 and 3 explore extreme (cold and hot) values of temperature. "
"Exercise 4 includes the presence of a potent denaturant (urea), and exercise"
" 5 is performed at a high pressure value."
msgstr ""
"理論編と演習1で学んだ内容から、演習2〜5は自分で実行できるはずです。違いは、各溶液条件を再現するために移行自由エネルギーの寄与が必要なことです。演習2と3では極端な低温・高温を調べ、演習4では強力な"
" Denaturant (urea) を加え、演習5では高圧を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:335
msgid ""
"This means that you will need to use the SASA module, as described in the "
"thoretical summary, to introduce the effect of temperature, pressure and "
"osmolyte concentration within the implicit solvent simulation."
msgstr ""
"理論概要で説明した SASA Module を使い、Implicit Solvent シミュレーションに温度・圧力・Osmolyte "
"濃度の効果を導入する必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:337
msgid ""
"The folder that you downloaded from [GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-"
"arsiccio/masterclass-22-13) contains 5 subfolders, one for each exercise. In"
" each subfolder, every file is ready to use, with the only exception of the "
"plumed.dat file, that you will need to write autonomously using the template"
" employed in exercise 1. Specifically, please monitor for each exercise the "
"radius of gyration and secondary structure content (alpha-helix, parallel "
"and antiparalle beta-sheet) of the protein, and print this information to a "
"file called COLVAR. You will also need to add a SASA_HASEL (hint: use "
"SASA_HASEL instead of SASA_LCPO, as the algorithm by Hasel et al. is faster)"
" and a BIASVALUE section to the plumed.dat file, as discussed in the "
"theoretical section."
msgstr ""
"[GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/masterclass-22-13) "
"から取得したフォルダには、各演習に対応する5つのサブフォルダがあります。plumed.dat 以外のファイルはそのまま使えます。plumed.dat "
"は演習1をひな形に自分で作成してください。各演習で Radius of Gyration と Secondary Structure "
"含有量（Alpha-helix、Parallel/Antiparallel Beta-sheet）を監視し、COLVAR "
"に出力します。また理論編の説明に従い、SASA_HASEL と BIASVALUE を追加します。Hasel "
"らのアルゴリズムの方が速いため、SASA_LCPO ではなく SASA_HASEL を使ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:340
msgid "You will need to perform the following steps:"
msgstr "必要な手順は次のとおりです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:342
msgid "install the software (PLUMED, AMBER)"
msgstr "ソフトウェア (PLUMED、AMBER) をインストールする。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:343
msgid ""
"clone the GitHub folder with input files: git clone "
"https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/masterclass-22-13"
msgstr ""
"入力ファイルの GitHub フォルダを Clone する：git clone https://github.com/andrea-"
"arsiccio/masterclass-22-13"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:344
msgid ""
"write a PLUMED file in each subfolder according to the example of Exercise 1"
" (hint: use the DeltaG-calculation.py script if needed! The README for the "
"script is available on [GitHub] (https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/DeltaG-"
"calculation), please have a look into it)"
msgstr ""
"演習1の例に従って、各サブフォルダに PLUMED ファイルを作成する。必要に応じて DeltaG-calculation.py "
"を使ってください。[GitHub] (https://github.com/andrea-arsiccio/DeltaG-calculation) "
"にあるスクリプトの README も確認してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:345
msgid "Run the simulations using the command:"
msgstr "次のコマンドでシミュレーションを実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:351
msgid ""
"Analyze the trajectories as already done during exercise 1 (plot the COLVAR "
"columns versus time, and use the script_rg_alpha.bash file to get a "
"representation of the conformational space explored)"
msgstr ""
"演習1と同様に Trajectory を解析する（COLVAR の各列を時間に対して描画し、script_rg_alpha.bash で探索した "
"Conformational Space を表す）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:353
msgid "You should ask yourself the following questions:"
msgstr "次の点を考えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:355
msgid ""
"what would you expect to occur at the protein structure at extreme values of"
" temperature/pressure/urea concentration? Are your expections reflected in "
"the simulation outputs?"
msgstr "極端な温度・圧力・urea 濃度では、タンパク質構造に何が起きると予想しますか？結果は予想を反映していますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:356
msgid ""
"would you observe similar phenomena also in 5-ns-long explicit solvent "
"calculations?"
msgstr "5 ns の Explicit Solvent 計算でも同様の現象が観測されるでしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:358
msgid "Final thoughts"
msgstr "最後に"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:360
msgid ""
"Through this tutorial we have learnt that the SASA module of PLUMED "
"implements two algorithms for the computation of the SASA (the faster "
"algorithm by Hasel et al., and the more accurate LCPO algorithm)."
msgstr ""
"この Tutorial では、PLUMED の SASA Module に2つの SASA 計算法（高速な Hasel らのアルゴリズムと、精度の高い "
"LCPO）が実装されていることを学びました。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:362
msgid ""
"We have found out that the SASA module can be used for introducing the SASA "
"as a collective variable or for monitoring the SASA, but it can furthermore "
"be employed to perform implicit solvent MD simulations."
msgstr ""
"SASA Module は SASA を Collective Variable として導入したり、監視したりするだけでなく、Implicit "
"Solvent MD にも利用できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:364
msgid ""
"Implicit solvent simulations with the SASA module are based on the concept "
"of free energy of transfer (where the 'transfer' occurs from pure water at "
"ambient temperature and pressure to an osmolyte solution at any desired "
"value of temperature and pressure)."
msgstr ""
"SASA Module による Implicit Solvent シミュレーションは、常温・常圧の純水から任意の温度・圧力の Osmolyte "
"溶液への「移行」を表す移行自由エネルギーに基づきます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:366
msgid ""
"Implicit solvent simulations have the advantage, compared to their explicit "
"solvent counterpart, to speed up conformational transitions, and allow a "
"faster exploration of conformational space."
msgstr ""
"Implicit Solvent は Explicit Solvent に比べ Conformational Transition "
"を速め、Conformational Space を迅速に探索できる利点があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:368
msgid ""
"NOTE: The Masterclass files with the solutions to the exercises are also "
"avilable on [GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-"
"arsiccio/masterclass-22-13-results), but please do the exercises on your own"
" before checking on the results!"
msgstr ""
"注：演習の解答ファイルも [GitHub](https://github.com/andrea-"
"arsiccio/masterclass-22-13-results) にありますが、結果を見る前に自分で取り組んでください。"
